<title>GERMANY: German 1996 crude steel output falls 5.4 percent.</title>
<headline>German 1996 crude steel output falls 5.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office gave the following data on pan-German steel production (in millions of tonnes):</p>
<p>		   1996	Pct change</p>
<p> Crude steel   39.80	   -5.4</p>
<p> Pig iron	27.72	   -7.6</p>
<p>		   Dec	Pct Change</p>
<p> Crude steel   3.29	  +17.2</p>
<p> Pig iron	2.40	  +14.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Percentage changes are against year-earlier figures. The office said the steel output decline that began in the fourth quarter of 1995 continued well into 1996, and started to turn around only in the final quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
